content::
The IS A relationship represents inheritance in Java, where one class inherits the properties and behaviors of another class. 
It indicates that a subclass is a specialized form of its superclass.
The IS A relationship is achieved using the extends keyword.
It promotes code reusability by allowing a child class to inherit fields and methods from a parent class.
command::
./tts.sh input.txt "90. What is the IS A relationship in OOPs Java.mp3"

content::
What are the different types of inheritance in Java?
Inheritance is of four types.
Single Inheritance. 
one subclass extends one superclass. 
Multilevel Inheritance.
subclass A extends B, and subclass B extends C, it creates a chain of inheritance called multilevel inheritance.
Hierarchical Inheritance.
multiple subclasses extend the same parent class.
Multiple Inheritance.
One subclass inherits from multiple parents.
Java does not support multiple inheritance with classes because it can cause ambiguity and complexity.
Java supports multiple inheritance through interfaces. A class can implement multiple interfaces.
command::
./tts.sh input.txt "91.What are the different types of inheritance in Java.mp3"

content::
inheritance has some limitations.
Tight coupling. Changes in the parent class can affect its child classes.
More complexity. Deep inheritance hierarchies can be difficult to understand and maintain.
No multiple inheritance with classes. A class cannot extend multiple classes in Java.
Less flexibility. Too much inheritance can make code harder to change. Sometimes composition is a better choice.
command::
./tts.sh input.txt "92.inheritance has some limitation.mp3"

content::
Inheritance is useful, but composition is often more flexible.
Composition. Part A relationship.
Why composition can be better.
Less coupling. Inheritance tightly connects the child to the parent.
More flexibility. Composition allows us to combine different objects without creating a large class hierarchy.
Easier to change. With composition, we can replace a component at runtime.
Inheritance is fixed. The parent-child relationship is decided at compile time.
constructors cannot be inherited in Java.
command::
