content::
Runtime polymorphism or Dynamic Method Dispatch is a feature where the method to execute is decided at runtime based on the actual object, not the reference type.
It allows a parent class reference to call an overridden method of a child class.
Achieved through method overriding.
A parent reference can refer to a child object.
The child's overridden method is executed at runtime.
