content::
The Java Collection Framework provides several interfaces for storing and managing data.
List. Stores elements in an ordered sequence and allows duplicates.
ArrayList, LinkedList.
Set. Stores unique elements and does not allow duplicates.
HashSet. LinkedHashSet. TreeSet.
Queue. Stores elements for processing in a specific order, usually First In First Out.
Examples. PriorityQueue, LinkedList.
Deque. A double-ended queue that allows adding and removing elements from both ends.
Examples. ArrayDeque, LinkedList.
Map. Stores data as key-value pairs. Keys are unique, but values can be duplicated.
HashMap, LinkedHashMap, TreeMap.
