stores data as key-value pairs.
Does not allow duplicate keys.
Duplicate values are allowed.
Each key is used to retrieve its corresponding value.
Common implementations include HashMap, LinkedHashMap, and TreeMap.
TreeMap. Maintains keys in ascending order by default.
Can use a custom Comparator for different sorting.
Does not allow null keys when using natural ordering.
