content::
EnumSet is a specialized Set implementation designed specifically for storing enum values.
It is part of the java util package and provides a high-performance way to work with sets of enum constants.
Features of EnumSet.
Can store only enum values.
Does not allow duplicate elements.
Maintains the natural order of enum constants. the order in which they are declared.
Does not allow null elements.
It is not synchronized.
It is generally more efficient than using a general-purpose HashSet for enum values.
It provides useful factory methods such as of, allOf, noneOf, and range.
